.TH XUR.STD.FMT 7 "2026-11-19" "xur 0.1.3" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.fmt \- format string syntax
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::fmt
documents the format string syntax used by
.BR io::print ,
.BR io::println ,
and string interpolation throughout xur.
.PP
This module is not imported directly; it is used internally by the I/O
functions.
.SH FORMAT SYNTAX
Each
.B {}
in the template is replaced by the next argument, displayed as a string.
.PP
Literal braces are written by doubling them:
.B {{
produces
.BR { ,
and
.B }}
produces
.BR } .
.PP
Unmatched braces are an error. Extra arguments beyond the number of
.B {}
placeholders are also an error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::io;

fn main() {
    io::println("hello, {}!", "world");
    io::println("{} + {} = {}", 1, 2, 3);
    io::println("literal braces: {{}}");
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std.io (7),
.BR xur.std.str (7)
